DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ffeettcchh functions are designed to copy small amounts of data from user-
     space of the current process.  If the user address is naturally aligned,
     then the operation will be performed atomically.  Otherwise it may fail
     or be performed non-atomically, depending on the platform.

     The ffeettcchh routines provide the following functionality:

     ffuubbyyttee()     Fetches a byte of data from the user-space address _b_a_s_e.
                  The byte read is zero-extended into the results variable.

     ffuuwwoorrdd()     Fetches a word of data (long) from the user-space address
                  _b_a_s_e.

     ffuuwwoorrdd1166()   Fetches 16 bits of data from the user-space address _b_a_s_e.
                  The half-word read is zero-extended into the results vari‐
                  able.

     ffuuwwoorrdd3322()   Fetches 32 bits of data from the user-space address _b_a_s_e.

     ffuuwwoorrdd6644()   Fetches 64 bits of data from the user-space address _b_a_s_e.

     ffuueewwoorrdd()    Fetches a word of data (long) from the user-space address
                  _b_a_s_e and stores the result in the variable pointed by _v_a_l.

     ffuueewwoorrdd3322()  Fetches 32 bits of data from the user-space address _b_a_s_e and
                  stores the result in the variable pointed by _v_a_l.

     ffuueewwoorrdd6644()  Fetches 64 bits of data from the user-space address _b_a_s_e and
                  stores the result in the variable pointed by _v_a_l.

     The callers of ffuuwwoorrdd(), ffuuwwoorrdd3322() and ffuuwwoorrdd6644() functions cannot dis‐
     tinguish between -1 read from userspace and function failure.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The ffuubbyyttee(), ffuuwwoorrdd(), ffuuwwoorrdd1166(), ffuuwwoorrdd3322(), and ffuuwwoorrdd6644() functions
     return the data fetched or -1 on failure.  The ffuueewwoorrdd(), ffuueewwoorrdd3322() and
     ffuueewwoorrdd6644() functions return 0 on success and -1 on failure.

